{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.8-flash", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 9, "dimension": 6, "mix_bound": 2, "mix_rounds": 24}, "seed": 1937260289, "solved": "failed", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": false, "verify_reason": "tensor-coordinate moment of degree 1 is nonzero", "reply": "To find the exact dependence among the simple tensors $T_i$, we note that the components of $T(t) = (M_A \\phi_{E_A}(t)) \\otimes (M_B \\phi_{E_B}(t)) \\otimes (M_C \\phi_{E_C}(t))$ are polynomials in $t$ with maximum degree:\n$$\\deg(T(t)) \\le \\max(E_A) + \\max(E_B) + \\max(E_C) = 2 + 5 + 7 = 14$$\n\nThe 16 parameters $t_i$ are the roots of the degree-16 even polynomial:\n$$P(t) = \\prod_{k=1}^{8} (t^2 - \\tau_k^2)$$\nwhere $\\{\\tau_k\\} = \\{10, 65, 291, 321, 331, 416, 445, 459\\}$.\n\nBy Cauchy's residue theorem / Lagrange interpolation, for any polynomial $f(t)$ with $\\deg(f) \\le 16 - 2 = 14$:\n$$\\sum_{i=0}^{15} \\frac{f(t_i)}{P'(t_i)} = 0$$\n\nThus, setting $\\lambda_i = \\frac{C}{P'(t_i)}$ gives $\\sum_{i=0}^{15} \\lambda_i T_i = 0$. Since $P(t)$ is even, $P'(-t) = -P'(t)$, guaranteeing that $\\lambda_i = -\\lambda_j$ whenever $t_i = -t_j$. \n\nChoosing $C = \\gcd(|P'(t_0)|, \\dots, |P'(t_{15})|)$ ensures that each coefficient simplifies to $\\lambda_i = [s_i, q_i] = \\frac{\\operatorname{sgn}(P'(t_i))}{|P'(t_i)| / C}$.\n\nEvaluating $q_i = |P'(t_i)| / C$ and $s_i = \\operatorname{sgn}(P'(t_i))$ for each $t_i$ in the displayed order:\n$t = [-416, 331, -331, 445, -459, 291, -321, -445, 459, 416, 10, -65, 65, -291, 321, -10]$\n\nyields the exact coefficients below.\n\n<answer>[[1,34919864272186595568181657600],[-1,1073867664687630718797824000],[1,1073867664687630718797824000],[1,1306126620953835056763699200],[-1,40251703276135805581977600],[1,2083161689086113880340480000],[1,970716670830491871248384000],[-1,1306126620953835056763699200],[1,40251703276135805581977600],[-1,34919864272186595568181657600],[1,32177968688984462204561326080000],[-1,180590855210960867